& [LedgerForm] is content-addressed and append-only
  + [ARL-001] AttentionLedger contains profile ledger_id frames sessions events and ledger_digest in deterministic collections
  + [ARL-002] frames are keyed by lowercase SHA-256 frame digest and stored bytes must validate that digest
  + [ARL-003] AttentionSessionState binds session_id sequence head_frame_digest head_generation head_status event_refs and session_digest
  + [ARL-004] AttentionLedgerEvent binds event_id session sequence command operation request digest response digest predecessor head optional successor head response status and event digest
  + [ARL-005] AttentionContinuation binds ledger identity and digest session sequence exact head generation digest status and latest event
  + [ARL-006] every form is strict JSON and JsonSchema capable

& [PureCommands] are closed
  + [ARL-007] new_attention_ledger deterministically creates one validated empty ledger
  + [ARL-008] OPEN validates one complete frame creates a previously absent session stores the frame and appends one open event
  + [ARL-009] APPLY accepts reconcile compact prepare or settle and resolves its base frame only from the current ledger head
  + [ARL-010] APPLY requires exact expected ledger digest session sequence and head frame digest before core dispatch
  + [ARL-011] the operation's own delta compaction or attestation bindings remain subject to existing core validation
  + [ARL-012] INSPECT READ_FRAME and READ_EVENT are pure exact-identity projections

& [TransitionRules] preserve history
  + [ARL-013] every admitted OPEN or APPLY appends exactly one event and advances session sequence exactly once
  + [ARL-014] applied reconciliation compaction candidate preparation or sealing stores and selects the returned successor frame
  + [ARL-015] buffered incomplete deferred revision-required and semantic-refusal responses retain the current head while recording exact outcome
  + [ARL-016] stale ledger stale sequence stale head duplicate session unknown session unknown frame unknown event digest mismatch collision or invalid ledger refuses with no successor
  + [ARL-017] no command removes or rewrites a frame event or prior session event reference
  + [ARL-018] equal repeated execution from equal input produces byte-equal output while replay against the successor is stale

& [LocalMCP] is explicit state custody
  + [ARL-019] a separate local STDIO server exposes exactly one tool continue_attention_session
  + [ARL-020] tool operations are open apply inspect read_frame and read_event and use the pure ledger command forms
  + [ARL-021] the server serializes mutations within one process but compare-and-set inputs remain mandatory
  + [ARL-022] every response includes a typed ledger result or typed fault and never relies on text summary as authority
  + [ARL-023] process state is volatile and server instructions declare that restart loses unpersisted sessions
  + [ARL-024] tool annotations are non-destructive idempotence depends on command and openWorld is false

& [Boundary] is a reentry locator not hidden truth
  + [ARL-025] continuation handles reduce repeated base-frame transport but full frames and events remain exactly readable
  + [ARL-026] ledger event admission records what Cantor returned and does not convert agreement refusal or imagination into external truth
  + [ARL-027] P0 performs no persistence model call network listener signing effect execution host registration or DreamFrame ledgering

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [ARL-A01] source SJS signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [ARL-A02] deterministic open stores one exact frame event session and continuation
  + [ARL-A03] compact apply resolves base internally advances the head and rejects stale replay
  + [ARL-A04] buffered and refused apply append distinct events without advancing the head
  + [ARL-A05] prepare and complete settle advance through candidate to sealed head
  + [ARL-A06] tampered ledger frame session event and root digests plus unknown reads refuse without successor
  + [ARL-A07] direct MCP and official client open apply inspect and read equal pure ledger behavior
  + [ARL-A08] formatting focused tests warnings-denied lint workspace regression manifest audit and scoped Git review pass

& [AuthorityBoundary] is local_in_memory_reentry_P0
  + permits pure ledger forms transitions validation tests one volatile local MCP server documentation proof and local process execution
  + excludes persistence database files network transport replication authentication deletion cleanup DreamFrame custody provider calls and effects

